  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(AMU conjecture). Let $S$ be a surface with negative Euler char-\nacteristic. If $\\varphi \\in \\operatorname{Mod}(S)$ acts by a pseudo-Anosov on some subsurface (including\n$S$ itself), show that there exists $p_{0}(\\varphi)$ such that the Witten–Reshetikhin–Turaev\nrepresentation $\\rho_{p}(\\varphi)$ has infinite order for $p \\geq p_{0}(\\varphi)$.",
